ates that was officially incorporated on February 14, 1980. Over the decades, it has evolved from a rural community into one of Utah's largest cities, reflecting broader trends of suburbanization and population growth in the late 20th century. As of the 2020 Census, the city boasts a population exceeding 136,000 residents, making it a vital part of the Salt Lake City metropolitan area. The establishment of West Valley City is emblematic of the demographic shifts occurring in the West, particularly as families and individuals sought affordable housing and community amenities outside urban cores.

